he door  one way the police when she called me I  heard all the knocking on the door and  stuff they were they were basically  breaking the door down I was scared  I did not know what to do as a matter I  did not want them to take him and do any  treatments or thought you know  like saying really that he really needs  dead thanks to this footage from the  camera Anna set up the raid on the knick  alliance made national news and prompted  a statewide audit of California's Child  Protective Services agencies a lot of  parental concern about our agency and  the reputation of the agency is based on  sensationalism and misunderstanding of  what we do  sherry Heller is head of Sacramento  County's Health and Human Services the  agency that oversees CPS she says  there's more to this story than meets  the eye but she can't and won't say  exactly what that is  I regret that I'm not able to answer  questions about specific cases because  both federal health care law and the  State of California's child welfare law  make it illegal for government agencies  involved in this kind of a case to talk  about anything that's in the case record  unless the court allows it and anyone  can petition the court we did file a  petition to open court records for this  case almost two months later there still  hasn't been a ruling and the records  remained sealed the secrecy by which CPS  operates is a massive problem because  when you when you have secrecy and  unchecked power you have a recipe for  corruption and abuse State Assemblyman  Tim Donnelly spearheaded the audit in  California after writing a letter to  Sherri Heller requesting more  information in the wake of the Nikolaev  raid and she basically wrote me back and  said we don't answer to Assemblyman we  don't answer the state legislature so in  between the lines what I heard was we  answer to no one the law is clear that  it's appropriate to act without a court  warrant if children are in imminent  danger of physical harm if you are given  the task of protecting children that's a  high bar and there's a great  responsibility that comes with that and  therefore I think that it's vital that  this agency no longer cloaked themselves  in secrecy Deana Hardwick found herself  and her children Meyer  in the secretive system when a social  worker removed her six and nine year old  daughters from her custody social  workers were brought in to investigate a  claim against her ex-husband that was  later found to be unsubstantiated  but once CPS enters your life it's often  hard to get them out my youngest  daughter ran into me during one of the  visits and said that she wasn't a let  them go home with me that night I asked  the social worker is it true and she  said it's what true and I said are you  not gonna let my kids go home with me  tonight and she said I told him if they  didn't visit with their dad the judge is  gonna put him in a home  Deanna and her children were shaken by  the social workers threat to put them in  a home but Deanna resolved to keep her  head down and her mouth shut hopeful  that her dealings with CPS were almost  over but the next day in court things  took a turn for the worse instead of her  admitting that she made the threat she  blamed the threat on me and the judge  believed her and she proceeded to build  a false claims and a false case against  me she sat me down and said basically  what I needed to do was to submit to her  I would never see my kids again  Deanna refused to submit and sign a  document corroborating the social  worker's version of events  she lost her court case and lost custody  of her children but things finally  turned around when she successfully sued  Orange County CPS and the social workers  who had targeted her the court records  are sealed but an unsuccessful appeal  mounted by CPS reveals that the jury  found social workers had lied falsified  evidence and suppressed exculpatory  evidence and done so with malice the  jury awarded Deanna 4.9 